Reader options: XML syntax (the xs flag) and scripting (the scripting
flag).
-- XMLSyntaxVoidEndTags xs --
A void element followed by its end tag, also with whitespace in between, is
one element.
-- in --
<p>a<br></br>b<br> </br>c<img src=i></img></p>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a<br />b<br /> c<img src="i" /></p></body></html>
-- XMLSyntaxSelfClosed xs --
Self-closing tags of non-void elements are empty elements.
-- in --
<div/>a<span/>b<p/>c
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><div></div>a<span></span>b<p></p>c</body></html>
-- XMLSyntaxScriptCDATA xs --
A CDATA section around the script contents, as XHTML writes it, is
removed, and the contents are wrapped again as needed.
-- in --
<script><![CDATA[if (a < b) x();]]></script><title><![CDATA[a<b]]></title>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><script>//<![CDATA[
if (a < b) x();
//]]></script><title>a&lt;b</title></head><body></body></html>
-- ScriptingNoscript scripting htmldiff nonidempotent --
Noscript contents are raw text, written unchanged without <, & or ]]>,
and escaped otherwise, which HTML parsers with scripting enabled read as
it is, and which is escaped again on every pass.
-- in --
<body><noscript>no js</noscript><noscript><b>x</b></noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><noscript>no js</noscript><noscript>&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt;</noscript></body></html>
-- warn --
42: escaped raw text noscript contents containing <, & or ]]> (HTML parsers with scripting enabled will read them as raw text when parsing the output)
